From c492f7006d0f2397fc7f9afc331521c99ea8210e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:37:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(fixtures): locate the stock on an existing vise

The locate took mates on the part only, so the stock could not be seated
on a vise that was already placed. The fixture collision checks and the
carried-workholding check then read a stock place that nobody set.

- fixture_locate: LocateSpec.body (Part default, Stock); stock_of;
  stock mates read in the stock's own pose; stock_lands refuses a turned
  stock re-fit that would leave the stock faces off the mates.
- LocatePart: with the stock held, the part moves and the stock follows,
  so the part keeps its place in the blank. One undo step.
- MCP: locate_part takes "body": "stock"; list_features lists a stock.
- UI: the locate form holds the stock by default when the setup has one
  ("Place by: Stock faces / Part faces"); picks pass over parts inside
  the stock while the stock is held.

Fixes #2173

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
